{{also|chel·a|chëla}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|la|chele}}, from {{der|en|grc|χηλή}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkilə/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkiːlə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-chela.wav|a=Southern England}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|chelae}}

# A [[pincer]]-like [[claw]] of a [[crustacean]] or [[arachnid]]. {{century|17}}
#* {{RQ:Browne Pseudodoxia Epidemica|III|5|passage=It happeneth often, I confess, that a lobster hath the '''chely''' or great claw of one side longer than the other {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1993|title=The Encyclopedia of Land Invertebrate Behaviour|page=232
|passage=The tail is curved up over the body and the pedipalps held forwards with the tip of the movable finger of the '''chela''' in contact with the sand.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Raymond T. Bauer|title=Remarkable Shrimps: Adaptations and Natural History of the Carideans|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=b8YHIsnod3EC&pg=PA26&dq=%22chela%22&hl=en&ei=PNgNTt_DHq7LmAW91-HKDg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CDcQ6AEwAjgK#v=onepage&q=%22chela%22&f=false|page=26
|passage=The two brushes on each '''chela''' snap open into semicircular fans, forming fine-mesh baskets that passively filter water.}}

